LeetCode 283 – Move Zeroes

class Solution:
    def moveZeroes(self, nums: List[int]) -> None:
        j=0
        for i in range(0,len(nums)):
            if nums[i]!=0:
                nums[i],nums[j]=nums[j],nums[i]
                j+=1

✅ Logic (For Loop)
💡 Idea
j scans every element.
i keeps track of the next position for a non-zero.
Whenever you find a non-zero:
Swap it with nums[i].
Increment i.
🧠 Memory Trick

"Scan with j, Fill with i."

for j in range(n):
    if nums[j] != 0:
        swap(nums[i], nums[j])
        i += 1

✅ Logic (While Loop)
💡 Idea
j manually scans the array.
i stores the next non-zero position.
If nums[j] is non-zero:
Swap.
Move i.
Always move j.
🧠 Memory Trick

"j always moves, i moves only after a swap."

while j < n:
    if nums[j] != 0:
        swap(nums[i], nums[j])
        i += 1
    j += 1
